     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "This is because outlier data can drastically skew the results and accuracy of the model. Outliers are typically identified and eliminated from the dataset before training the model to ensure more accurate predictions."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Data points that are rare or abnormal in comparison to the rest of the data"
